extraction_notes: "Transcribed from Rifts World Book 3: England p.71-72, the optional R.C.C. of a creature the book offers as a villain and leaves to the Game Master for player use; Nate ruled 2026-11-12 that it gets a class row beside its creature row. The class takes the player character''s spell set (ten temporal spells of choice plus the eleven named, then one temporal spell of any level and two conventional spells of levels 1-8 each level); the NPC set stays on the creature row. Protection Circle: Lesser, as the book names it, is held as Protection Circle: Simple. Temporal spell rows stand as the catalog holds them; no spell row was added or changed. XP: the raider''s own table printed on p.152. All bonuses are half until sixth level: stored as half, rounded down, with the remainder added at level six, so the level-six totals equal the creature row''s full figures (+5 strike, +7 parry and dodge, +6 initiative, +5 roll and pull punch, +3 save vs psionics and magic, +7 vs Horror Factor). Attacks: three hand to hand at level one, one more at levels 4, 7, 11 and 15, as the creature row records for a player character. The +6 to strike with energy blasts and the magic attacks per melee are special-ability prose. occ_group magic and men_of_arms false, from the book filing the class under the Temporal Magic heading. Language: Dragonese is printed with no percentage, so it is stored at the catalog''s rate rather than as a fixed figure; the three other languages are a choose of Language: Other. Not stored: the energy pistol and energy rifle. Attributes, M.D.C., P.P.E., I.S.P., Horror Factor, psionics and starting money agree with the creature row temporal-raider; the creature row cites p.71-73 because it also carries the NPC treasure notes."
