# Temporal Raider

## Lore

A supernatural alien energy being that commands dimensional and temporal magic: a demonic looking eight foot (2.4 m), 700 pound (315 kg) giant with an armor plated mega-damage body, claws and a terrible temper. The bald head looks masked in brushed silver metal, which is part of its body, and metal-like plates cover the fingers, hands, forearms, neck and chest; skin is light grey or blue-grey. Raiders feed on the life energy of other creatures, are fearsome fighters, tacticians and thieves, and will strike even the Splugorth with hit and run tactics. They find humans kindred spirits and occasionally take them as apprentices in temporal magic, bound to six years of servitude and to secrecy. Most are obsessed with wealth and power and become warlords, guild heads, counselors or kings, though few settle anywhere for more than a generation or two. Life span unknown, suspected 10,000 years or more.

## GM Notes

The temporal raider makes for great non-player villains. NPCs are 7th to 12th level (average 1D6+6) and know all temporal magic spells, all summoning magic, Protection Circles Simple and Superior, Tongues, Eyes of Thoth, Shadow Meld, Time Slip, Negate Magic, Mystic Portal, Close Rift, Dimensional Portal, Teleport: Lesser and Superior, plus 12 spells from levels one through eight, and two more of any level from level 9. An NPC has five hand to hand or psionic attacks per melee (or ten light or five heavy blasts, or two magic attacks), one more at levels 11 and 15, and the full bonuses. Older NPC raiders hide treasure troves in 1D6 dimensions, each with 3D6x10,000 credits, 2D6 million credits in gems and as much again in artifacts and magic; they carry 1D6 million credits.
', 'published', 'data-script'
